==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 15.3 Update|Version 15.3]], she was called Black Okame.
*An Okame or Otafuku is a mask used in ''[[wikipedia:Kyōgen|Kyōgen]]'' theater to represent a positive female and good luck-bringer being; the distaff counterpart to [[wikipedia:Hyottoko|Hyottoko]].
*Her gender is confirmed in her Korean description, which uses the feminine pronoun 그녀의 ''geunyeoui'' (her). In every version except [[BCEN]], Masked Okame is also stated to have a maiden's heart.
*Masked Okame can be seen as a foil to [[Hannya]]. Where Hannya's mask is a symbol of bitterness and jealousy, Okame's represents felicity and blessings.
*As a symbol of innocent maidenhood, Masked Okame appears to represent the virtue of chastity among the Tier 2 [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]].
*The word Gaō in Masked Okame's Japanese name, Okame Gaō (阿亀我王), doesn't mean anything on its own and is just a pun on ''kao'' (顔), meaning "face", though it can rarely also be a person's name. It consists of the kanji for "ego" or "self-assertion" (我) and "king" (王).
*Hannya's Japanese description mentions that she consumes the souls of those who cannot gain enlightenment, with the term used, ''jōbutsu'' (成仏) specifically referring to attaining Buddhahood. This theme of Buddhism is continued with Masked Okame's stage names:
**[[The Pure Land (Merciless)|Courts of Torment]]'s Japanese name is Narakumon (奈落門), which translates to "[[wikipedia:Naraka|Naraka]] Gate". A Naraka is the Buddhist equivalent of Hell.
**"[[The Pure Land (Merciless)|Pure Land]]" is a concept in Mayahayan Buddhism, its many traditions and teachings falling into the branch of [[wikipedia:Pure Land Buddhism|Amidism/Pure Land Buddhism]]. Reaching the [[wikipedia:Pure Land|Pure Land]] is the final goal of Amidism and is tantamount to attaining enlightenment.
**The opposite of the Pure Land is the land of the living, also called the Impure Land, which appears in [[Heaven and Hell (Merciless)|Heaven and Hell]]'s Japanese name.
**[[Okame's Teahouse (Merciless)|Okame's Teahouse]]'s Japanese name, Meido Kissa OKAME (冥土喫茶OKAME), has a pun on ''meido kissa'', which would normally mean "maid café", but the stage's name spells ''meido'' as 冥土, meaning the underworld; the world of the dead. Like the Pure Land, 冥土 is a Buddhist term.
*Masked Okame was the first Tier 2 Advent Boss to receive [[:Category:Awakening Stages|Awakening Stages]] for its [[Medusa Cat (Rare Cat)|drop]].

